fix(slack-canvas-sync): close a fence in mention handling the same way as everywhere else

The mention canonicalizer closed a code fence on any line of backticks or
tildes that started with the opener, the same bug CodeRabbit found in the
validator on #428. It now uses the shared closesFence (same character, at
least as long), so a mention after a non-closing line stays inside the code.

